{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>She is more righteous than I.</b> According to what we wrote above, that the reason they sentenced her to be burned was because the court of Shem had decreed concerning Gentile harlotry — once it was revealed that she had lain with Judah, she is more righteous than Judah, for Judah did not know that she was his daughter-in-law and she was in the presumption of being a Gentile woman, yet he lay with her and transgressed the decree of the court of Shem. And that is his saying ״צָדְקָה מִמֶּנִּי.״ And this is the measure of the verse: she is righteous in her words, and consequently righteous in her judgment, and further she is more than me in righteousness for the reason I have written. And Judah was not held liable for his admission that he lay with her in the presumption of her being a Gentile woman, since in truth she was not a Gentile woman — and this matter resembles one who intends to eat a piece of forbidden fat and a piece of garlic is in his hand [instead]." "And if you will say: after all, at the time of the act she was in the presumption of a Gentile woman when he lay with her, so why did he transgress the decree of the court? To this our Rabbis of blessed memory already explained (Genesis Rabbah, parashah 85) that from HaShem are a man's steps, and He arranges the plots to bring hidden things to light. Go out and learn what we explained in parashat Vayehi on the verse (Genesis 49:9) ״גּוּר אַרְיֵה״ etc." "<b>Because therefore I did not give her</b> etc. Meaning, according to what he said ״she is more righteous than I,״ he concluded that she also did not act promiscuously, for her reason was because ״I did not give her to Shelah my son.״ She saw that her hope was lost; therefore she did this thing." "<b>Or</b> it may intend to say that he was the cause of her doing so, in that he did not give her to Shelah, and that is his saying <b>she is righteous</b> — she is [righteous] in her deeds, <b>more than me</b> — meaning, from my side: I was the cause for her, ״because I did not give her״ etc."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:47:02.218533717Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}